4	/// Each gated, levelled or de-essed clip's reference level (spec §11 AU-41,
5	/// AU-42, AU-66): the clip's `ClipLoudness` reading — the Volume section's
6	/// Loudness figure, pre-fader, over the window that plays, in the export's
7	/// layout through pan · fold · pick — which the three stages' relative
8	/// thresholds (and the leveller's target) are added to.
9	///
10	/// **Measured once per (cache folder, plan text, the clip's channel
11	/// matrix).** A trim moves the plan and a pan or a pick moves the matrix, so
12	/// either measures again; a property edit that moves neither reads the memo.
13	/// A PENDING answer — no loudness file yet, or no cache folder — is never
14	/// memoised, and the media files are read through a fresh `MediaCacheLoader`
15	/// each time (it would hold a miss as pending), so the first ask after the
16	/// file lands answers measured with no invalidation. Loaded files are kept
17	/// per cache folder until that media's `loudness` post.
18	///
19	/// **The leveller's curves** (AU-66 (e), `curves`) are made beside L from
20	/// the same reading and the clip's speech mask, one per response its base and
21	/// its ends name, and memoised the same way with the `media.speech` they used:
22	/// a change of it makes them again. Without spans they are pending while
23	/// speech detection can still land a VAD file, and unmeasurable when it
24	/// cannot (`SileroVAD.isAvailable`, read on each call).
25	///
26	/// **The watch.** A `loudness` cache post (a landing or a withdrawal) drops
27	/// that media's memo, curves and loaded file, then posts
28	/// `.reversedMediaDidChange` for each open document with a gate, leveller or
29	/// de-esser on that media, so its editor rebuilds with no edit — the plan did
30	/// not change, the disk did. A `speech` post drops its curves and rebuilds
31	/// each document levelling it.
32	///
33	/// **The export's wait** (`wait`) polls every 0.1 s, never on main, until no
34	/// clip it names has a pending level or curve, the caller cancels, or the
